From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:39:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/46] Rename the browser in the remaining Android strings

Patch 0038 renamed the launcher entry, widget titles, About page and menu description, and
said at the time that it covered what was visible in the app. Using the build turned up plenty
it missed: Restart Chrome, Open Chrome menu, Chrome tips, Use Chrome by default, and the
descriptions of preloading and Incognito locking.

337 strings across the Android string files now say Bare.

Three kinds of mention are deliberately left alone. Google products keep their names, so
Chrome Web Store, Google Chrome and ChromeOS are untouched. Strings describing Google features
this build removes, sign-in, sync, Gemini and activity linking, keep saying Chrome: renaming
them would put this browser's name on things it cannot do, which is worse than text that never
renders. And translator descriptions are not user visible, so they are not worth churning.

Changing a message invalidates its translations, so these strings fall back to English in
other languages until retranslated. That is unavoidable in a rename.
